WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.237
First things first.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.739
Time to go fishing.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.876
I hope to get
some-- some eels.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.810
Some eels?

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.245
Yeah, a Conger eel.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.180
We have big conger eels here.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.216
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
Of course, David wants

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.851
to go fishing for conger eels.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.087
They're powerful and
enormous, just like David's

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.123
competitive Croatian spirit.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.057
Is that yours?

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:24.924
Yes.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:25.892
Yes, it's my beauty.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:26.826
That is a beautiful boat.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:27.861
Thank you.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.329
Oh, I'm so excited, honestly.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.564
You're not going fishing
from my sailing boat.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.699
What?

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.067
We're not going fishing
from my sailing boat.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.635
We're going fishing
with my father.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.569
Stop it.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.570
In that dingy?

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:38.505
Yeah.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.506
It's a traditional
way of fishing.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.774
Yeah, but hold on a minute.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.675
Ah, this is for joy-- for fun.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.844
But let's talk about
comfortable first.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.979
Is that really your father?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:46.746
Yeah.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:47.580
Good morning.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.214
Welcome.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.549
Good to see you.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.450
Are you serious we're
going fishing in that?

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.418
Yes.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.719
There's me thinking
we're on this

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:53.953
beautiful, glamorous
sailboat that belongs

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.488
to David and his family.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:01:00.660
But no, [bleep] he wants me
to become Croatian quickly.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:01.828
Should we set sail?

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.796
Or set sink?

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.369
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
People told me

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:13.306
Croatia was like Italy, but none
of my vacations on Amalfi Coast

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:18.611
had me fishing in a boat not
much bigger than a bathtub.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.114
David's dad set a
line of baited hooks

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:25.752
at dawn to hopefully
catch a conger eel.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.720
Just be careful for the hooks.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.621
Big hooks.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.355
Be very careful.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.757
It's a dangerous thing.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.525
GORDON RAMSEY: (VOICEOVER)
[bleep] This line has

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.028
100 hooks set 3 meters apart.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.696
[bleep] Big hooks.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.299
Grab the wrong spot and
you've gone from fisherman

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.700
to catch of the day.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.902
Little bend on your
knees so it will be easier.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:43.903
Gotcha.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.771
It's a work out and a half.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:45.805
Yep.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.240
It's good for your shoulders.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.408
There's one on there.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.108
Hm?

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:49.776
There's one on there.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.543
Yeah?

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.411
It's a big one.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.612
Yes.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.047
When you start feeling
that tug all of a sudden,

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.715
it's an indication
there's a conger.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.553
That's heavy on there.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.554
Get up.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.288
Get up.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.823
You can feel it.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.824
Wow.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.726
[non-english speech]

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.994
That's a big one.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.462
I'm talking about a
girth of your knee.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.264
I mean, they're thick,
and they're strong,

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.632
and they're powerful.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:13.500
There's another one.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.201
There's another
one down there.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.169
Yes, it's a big one.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.604
It's a big one?

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.041
[bleep] I can feel it.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.376
That is mahoosive.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.378
There's one more on here.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.347
What the [bleep] is under there?

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:30.350
The tug of a conger eel
with a hand line is huge.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.786
You can really feel
that thing fighting you.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.823
That's heavy on there.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.859
[bleep] There is that adrenaline
because you're pulling like mad

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.661
and you can feel
it tug, tug, tug.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:42.595
Here she comes.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.329
He's coming.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.731
It's tugging like mad.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.033
GORDON RAMSEY: (VOICEOVER)
This line isn't budging.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.235
David says eels
here can wait nearly

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:52.171
30 pounds, which is much
bigger than anything

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.107
I've pulled in so far.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.041
That is massive.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.209
It's a big one.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.818
Wow.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.886
That's a beauty.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.488
The size of that thing.

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:10.924
GORDON RAMSEY: (VOICEOVER) After
my Croatian Cross Fit workout,

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.959
I'm definitely
ready for a break.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.093
Oh.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.562
GORDON RAMSEY:
(VOICEOVER) I just

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:16.930
hope my arms have enough
strength left to lift the eel

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:20.066
from my plate to my mouth.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.336
We made some conger eel pate.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:26.839
Mm.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.941
It's silky--

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.208
Wow.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.843
--and very tasty,
a little bit buttery.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.613
I had no idea
it can be finessed

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.714
to that level of a pate.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.282
It's really good.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.352
Our limit in the kitchen, you
know, it's all in our heads.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.421
An amazing start to my
journey, let me tell you.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.090
I'll come back at the end of the
week and we'll cook together.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.258
Yeah?

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.793
I'll give you a
run for your money.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.094
Thank you.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.096
Now can you get me
off this bloody boat?

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:53.199
I never thought a conger
eel could set the bar.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.301
Based on the flavor
of that pate,

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.737
I think this guy has got
other tricks up his sleeve.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:04:01.207
This is going to be
a tough final cook.

